// A case dispatch omits when THREE things hold at once: the subject is a FIELD
// place, the chain has THREE OR MORE named-case arms, and there is no authored
// `_` arm. Removing any one of the three makes the identical program check.
// Reduced from `samples/cli/basics/brightness_control`.
//
// Three independently sufficient rescues, each a one-token control:
//
//   final arm `Command::C`  -> `_`            checks   (holds at 3 and 4 arms)
//   subject `self.command`  -> a local        checks   (same arms, same sum)
//   three named arms        -> two            checks   (see the caveat below)
//
// The caveat on the third: with no `_`, exhaustiveness forces the arm count to
// equal the case count -- a short named list is rejected outright by the
// coverage check -- so the two-arm point necessarily also has a two-case sum.
// "Two arms" and "two-case sum" could not be separated. The other two rescues
// have clean one-token controls and do not share that confound.
//
// Ruled out, each in both directions: PAYLOAD BINDINGS (a payload-free chain
// omits, a payload-bearing chain checks); ARITHMETIC in an arm target (removing
// it still omits, keeping it still checks); WHICH arm carries the payload (the
// payload-bearing arm moved last still omits, so what matters about the final
// arm is its `_`-ness, not its payload-freeness); being the machine body's TAIL
// (moved into a later state it still omits, reported at that state); CONSTANT
// versus DYNAMIC subject (a constant field omits and a dynamic field omits; a
// constant local checks and a dynamic local checks -- so const folding does not
// explain the local exemption); SUM CASE COUNT alone (a four-case sum checks
// with a `_` present); and SUCCESSOR COLLAPSING (three distinct successors still
// check, one shared successor still omits).
//
// The reading that "the terminator admits an ordered guarded chain ending in
// its authored `_` arm" is INCOMPLETE rather than wrong: chains with no `_` at
// all are admitted when the subject is a local, or when there are two arms. Do
// not pin a repair on `_`-termination alone.
//
// Separately found while measuring, and NOT this gap: passing a SUM-TYPED value
// as a state parameter omits at `state graph: terminator: jump successor:
// parameter transfer` whether or not a `_` arm is present. That blocked
// measuring the "parameter subject" axis and is its own defect.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Command {
    case A;
    case B;
    case C;
}

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    command: Command;
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console {
    self.command = Command::A;

    transition self.command {
        Command::A -> done()
        Command::B -> done()
        Command::C -> done()
    }

    state done(&mut self) {
        self.console.exit_process(0);
    }
}
